              "date": "2025-10-21T08:40",
              "body": "Physical, 52 y/o man.\n\nSince last fall: no ER or hospital. Back pain steady, pain clinic still writing oxycodone 5 mg prn. Omeprazole daily. Alcohol unchanged overall per him; wife had told our front desk she is worried.\n\nROS negative for jaundice, abdominal swelling, GI bleeding, chest pain, shortness of breath, falls.\n\nExam: VS as charted, weight stable. Anicteric. Neck no masses. Heart regular rate, no murmurs. Lungs clear bilaterally. Abd soft, liver not palpable, no ascites. Ext without edema. No tremor. Skin no rashes.\n\nAUDIT-C 12. PHQ-9 2.\n\nA/P\nPrevention: flu, updated COVID and Tdap (no tetanus record in his old chart, he can't recall one) today. LDCT and FIT again. Lipids, A1c in the draw.\nAUD / alcoholic liver disease: advice repeated, he declines referral. Labs.\nLow back pain: stable.\nSee him in early 2026."
